From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiBootManagerLib: do not enumerate USB NICs as boot options

BmEnumerateBootOptions() creates a boot option for every LoadFile handle,
which includes the PXE/HTTP-boot instances riding the BMC's USB CDC
network gadget - the Redfish host interface. That is a management link
with no boot server behind it: an attempt would sit through a full
DHCP timeout, and every enumeration pokes the gadget's network stack.

The existing PlatformBm prune (edk2-platforms 0005) deletes such options
after PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole's refresh, but the Boot Manager UI
calls EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption() itself and recreates them
inside Setup. Filter at the source instead: skip LoadFile handles whose
device path carries both a USB node and a MAC node. USB mass storage has
no MAC node and platform NICs (RP1 GEM) have no USB node, so both keep
their options. The 0005 prune stays as cleanup for options persisted by
older firmware.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform policy]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
index e3d34af..724cf5e 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
@@ -2225,6 +2225,48 @@ BmMatchPartitionDevicePathNode (
   return FALSE;
 }
 
+/**
+  Check whether the device path is a network interface carried over USB.
+
+  A USB NIC's device path contains both a USB node and a MAC node. USB mass
+  storage carries no MAC node; a PCI or platform NIC carries no USB node.
+
+  @param DevicePath  The device path to check. NULL returns FALSE.
+
+  @retval TRUE   The device path is a network interface behind a USB node.
+  @retval FALSE  It is not.
+**/
+STATIC
+BOOLEAN
+BmIsUsbNicDevicePath (
+  IN EFI_DEVICE_PATH_PROTOCOL  *DevicePath
+  )
+{
+  EFI_DEVICE_PATH_PROTOCOL  *Node;
+  BOOLEAN                   HasMac;
+  BOOLEAN                   OverUsb;
+
+  if (DevicePath == NULL) {
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
+  HasMac  = FALSE;
+  OverUsb = FALSE;
+  for (Node = DevicePath; !IsDevicePathEnd (Node); Node = NextDevicePathNode (Node)) {
+    if (DevicePathType (Node) != MESSAGING_DEVICE_PATH) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_USB_DP) {
+      OverUsb = TRUE;
+    } else if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_MAC_ADDR_DP) {
+      HasMac = TRUE;
+    }
+  }
+
+  return (BOOLEAN)(HasMac && OverUsb);
+}
+
 /**
   Emuerate all possible bootable medias in the following order:
   1. Removable BlockIo            - The boot option only points to the removable media
@@ -2401,6 +2443,17 @@ BmEnumerateBootOptions (
       continue;
     }
 
+    //
+    // Skip network interfaces carried over USB. On this platform the only
+    // USB NIC is the BMC's CDC network gadget - the Redfish host interface,
+    // a management link with no boot server behind it. Filtering at
+    // enumeration (rather than pruning afterwards) keeps such options out
+    // of every refresh, including the ones the Boot Manager UI triggers.
+    //
+    if (BmIsUsbNicDevicePath (DevicePathFromHandle (Handles[Index]))) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
     Description = BmGetBootDescription (Handles[Index]);
     BootOptions = ReallocatePool (
                     sizeof (EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION) * (*BootOptionCount),
